Oh yes, the daggers of death.  More fearsome than most 
artifacts they are.  

> So, the silver sabre is good, but I probably need another weapon.

Well, I had good experiences with two silver sabers, and 
even two chrysknives are nice.  My favourite from the 
current menue would be Stormbringer, of course.  

> SB is a broadsword and a nasty character, but I would fear for my
> pet.  

Unless it's for sentimental reasons, I would recommend 
ditching your pet and run with Stormbringer.  Its 
level-draining makes trolls much less annoying, and you 
can tin Olog-Hais easily enough.  Btw, Stormy can easily 
be utilized to buy maximum protection (naked AC -10) if 
you really want.  You can buy at mine town or in the valley.  

> Should I wish for FB or GS?  I guess I won't be getting any
> more weapon slot upgrades since I've been crowned.

If you want to use some wishes (remember:  The more artifacts 
already created, the lower the chance of getting a wished-for 
artifact), Grayswandir would be my personal favourite (FB tends 
to freeze and shatter valuable potions); however you should keep 
in mind that you're restricted in saber as well as in long sword.  

> I have a /oW 0:1 and 2 blessed magic lamps, so that's a probable
> 7 wishes at my beck.
> I don't care about conduct, I'll wish for anything.  I started
> the game with a +3 SDSM.  This was the result of a reckless
> fountain quaff that put Tsingi the wizard into go mode.  The /oW
> started out at 0:2, used one on the HoB.
> 
> So, I have lots of wishes.

Wish for amulets of live-saving.  They're quite useful.  
And wish for magic markers; keep one and a blank spellbook 
at hand, and utilize the rest for scrolls of teleport.  Oh, 
and I wouldn't say no to an additional wand of death.  *Very* 
useful stuff, in particular in the endgame, when your power 
points are down.  Remember to carry some charging with you.  
And you might want to genocide Ls, hs and ;s to make life 
easier.  

