> I could advance bare hand, divination and clerical now.
> Clerical would get me better remove curse, but other than
> that there is no reason to up it, unless spells perform
> better if the skill level is higher.  Do they?

Some do, but the real power for your wizard lies in 
the attack business.  It's nice to have remove curse, 
but you'll carry a bunch of !oHW anyway.  The divination 
and clerical business is not really important.  

> I will work on advancing healing and matter.  

Healing is important, due to the missing spell mentioned 
above.  

> Started with
> Extra healing but could rarely use it.  Healing is a very
> recent acquirement and hasn't been used much.  Gehennom may
> change that keeping Rollins in shape.  

Unlikely.  Your natural regeneration is so high and the 
healing power of extra healing is so low it is rarely worth 
using it instead of an offensive spell.  It would be very 
useful if you plan to keep your pet, though.  

> Amulets
> g - an uncursed amulet of magical breathing named (being worn)

Un-naming an object works by giving it the name " " 
(i.e., one blank), if you wanted to do so.  

> b - a blessed bag of holding

You might want to hide the bag in a sack, thus preventing 
it to be unblessed.  

> o - an uncursed oilskin sack

Even better than a sack.. 

> I usually wear a =oSD

You really, really want to improve your Strength.  Hence, 
eat any giant you may come across (tinning them reduces 
their nutrition value but keeps the Str improvement).  

> Potions
> - a potion of holy water
> - 5 potions of unholy water
> - 2 uncursed potions of confusion
> - 6 uncursed potions of gain level
> - 3 cursed potions of gain level

I would curse the !oGL; very useful once you got the amulet.  
Secondly, gather wands of teleport and digging.  I know that 
you can use spells instead, but the AoY makes spellcasting 
expensive, and at least for teleport you can't utilize the 
drop-cast-pickup routine.  The way out of Gehennom can be 
brought down to <1000 turns (<400 if you're lucky) utilizing 
controlled teleport and ~10 cursed !oGL, and death-fingering 
Rodney.  I usually teleport/quaff my way up to Lvl 1 without 
meeting Rodney more than once or twice (my last three ascensions, 
IIRC, had Rodney listed as killed twice, which seems almost 
the minimum[1]).  

As a general remark, your character seems well-prepared, 
up to the HP issue.  But of course, most good chars die 
a YASD rather than YAAD (and no, I won't tell what my last 
healer did on the astral plane, right next to pestilence ;-)),  
so be very careful.  

